config BR2_PACKAGE_AIC8800
	bool "aic8800"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Out-of-tree driver + firmware for the AICSemi AIC8800D80
	  (WiFi 6 + BT 5.4) as found in the ROCK 4D's onboard Quectel
	  FCU760K module, USB-attached. Radxa's packaging of the vendor
	  driver, pinned by commit, with Radxa's debian/patches applied
	  (the stock source does not build on kernel 6.1).

	  Builds aic_load_fw.ko (firmware uploader; binds the cold
	  a69c:8d80 device, uploads firmware, chip re-enumerates as
	  a69c:8d81), aic8800_fdrv.ko (cfg80211 fullmac WiFi -> wlan0)
	  and aic_btusb.ko (BlueZ hci0). All three autoload via USB
	  modalias; firmware is read from
	  /lib/firmware/aic8800_fw/USB/aic8800D80 via filp_open.

	  https://github.com/radxa-pkg/aic8800
